    "readout_text": "To evaluate the expression:\n\n$$\n2^3 - 1^3 + 4^3 - 3^3 + 6^3 - 5^3 + \\dots + 18^3 - 17^3,\n$$\n\nwe observe that the terms are grouped in pairs of the form:\n\n$$\n(2n)^3 - (2n - 1)^3,\n$$\n\nwhere $ n $ ranges from 1 to 9. This is because the last pair is $ 18^3 - 17^3 $, and $ 18 = 2 \\times 9 $, so there are 9 such pairs.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Use the identity for the difference of cubes\n\nRecall the identity:\n\n$$\na^3 - b^3 = (a - b)(a^2 + ab + b^2).\n$$\n\nLet $ a = 2n $ and $ b = 2n - 1 $. Then $ a - b = 1 $, so:\n\n$$\n(2n)^3 - (2n - 1)^3 = (2n)^2 + (2n)(2n - 1) + (2n - 1)^2.\n$$\n\nNow expand each term:\n\n- $ (2n)^2 = 4n^2 $,\n- $ (2n)(2n - 1) = 4n^2 - 2n $,\n- $ (2n - 1)^2 = 4n^2 - 4n + 1 $.\n\nAdding these together:\n\n$$\n4n^2 + (4n^2 - 2n) + (4n^2 - 4n + 1) = 12n^2 - 6n + 1.\n$$\n\nSo, each pair simplifies to:\n\n$$\n(2n)^3 - (2n - 1)^3 = 12n^2 - 6n + 1.\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Sum over all pairs\n\nWe now compute the total sum:\n\n$$\n\\sum_{n=1}^{9} (12n^2 - 6n + 1) = 12\\sum_{n=1}^{9} n^2 - 6\\sum_{n=1}^{9} n + \\sum_{n=1}^{9} 1.\n$$\n\nUse standard summation formulas:\n\n- $ \\sum_{n=1}^{9} n^2 = \\frac{9 \\cdot 10 \\cdot 19}{6} = 285 $,\n- $ \\sum_{n=1}^{9} n = \\frac{9 \\cdot 10}{2} = 45 $,\n- $ \\sum_{n=1}^{9} 1 = 9 $.\n\nNow compute:\n\n$$\n12 \\cdot 285 = 3420, \\quad -6 \\cdot 45 = -270, \\quad +9.\n$$\n\nAdd them together:\n\n$$\n3420 - 270 + 9 = 3159.\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{3159}\n$$",
